 7. 🎥 Ellison&#x27;s California pressure point worked 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 David Ellison speaks at CinemaCon in Las Vegas in April. Photo: Chris Pizzello/AP The terms and timing of Paramount Skydance's settlement with state attorneys general were the byproduct of clever maneuvering by CEO David Ellison, who identified a unique point of leverage over the plaintiffs' ringleader, California Attorney General Rob Bonta (D), Axios' Sara Fischer reports. 

 Why it matters: Bonta lost political support for his lawsuit after it became clear Paramount was serious about leaving California and taking thousands of jobs with it. That put pressure on him to settle quickly ahead of Paramount's ticking fee deadline of Sept. 30. By late August, a slew of high-profile California Democrats, including Gov. Gavin Newsom, L.A. Mayor Karen Bass and Democratic gubernatorial nominee Xavier Becerra, had called on Bonta to settle.

 Newsom played a key role in brokering settlement talks with Bonta. More later today in Sara Fischer's weekly Axios Media Trends. Get it here . 

 
 
